      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_District%2C_San_Francisco",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Nearly destroyed in the 1906 earthquake, the district’s skyscrapers survived and were rebuilt by 1910.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_District%2C_San_Francisco",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Late 1920s Neo‑Gothic towers like the Standard Oil Building rose to 300‑400 feet, reshaping the skyline.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
